# 14. Compliance Requirements

## Purpose

This section establishes the mandatory governance requirements for all System Objectives and objective documentation within the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA).

Its purpose is to ensure consistent application of the Objective Governance framework across the entire objective library.

---

## General Compliance

Every System Objective and objective category document shall comply with:

- The Project Charter.
- The System Objective Specification (SOS).
- This Objective Governance document.
- Applicable engineering governance documents.

---

## Mandatory Requirements

Every System Objective shall:

- Possess a unique objective identifier.
- Belong to one approved objective category.
- Follow the approved lifecycle.
- Maintain complete traceability.
- Comply with the approved versioning standard.
- Undergo the required review and approval process.
- Maintain documented engineering justification.
- Preserve historical records throughout its lifecycle.

---

## Documentation Compliance

Objective documentation shall:

- Follow the approved repository structure.
- Use the approved documentation templates where applicable.
- Maintain consistent terminology.
- Record revisions and approvals.
- Preserve relationships with related engineering artifacts.

---

## Governance Compliance

Compliance shall be evaluated during:

- Objective creation.
- Objective review.
- Objective approval.
- Objective revision.
- Objective retirement.

Non-compliance shall be documented and resolved before approval unless an approved exception has been granted through the project's governance process.

---

## Compliance Records

Compliance activities shall maintain records of:

- Evaluation date.
- Scope of evaluation.
- Compliance findings.
- Identified non-conformities.
- Corrective actions.
- Approval status.

---

## Engineering Perspective

Compliance is a mechanism for ensuring consistency, quality, and engineering discipline.

Its purpose is not merely to enforce rules but to preserve the integrity, traceability, and long-term reliability of the AVIA engineering repository.
